gametitle=The Godfather (PAL) [SLES-53967] 9C5C1478
// PCSX2 cheats for the European PAL disc (CRC 9C5C1478).
// Sources: Codejunkies UK Action Replay MAX list for The Godfather (PAL), decrypted with omniconvert's AR MAX algorithm
//   (mirrored at https://gamehacking.org/game/101576); Max All Skill Levels ported from Code Master's NTSC-U CodeBreaker codes;
//   custom code-cave cheats made for this pack. All patch addresses checked against the PAL ELF SLES_539.67.
// Status: [UNTESTED] = not yet confirmed in game. Do not enable two cheats that say they replace each other.

[Infinite Health]
author=Codejunkies (AR MAX, decrypted by IRISHDEVELOPERDEV)
description=[UNTESTED] (do not combine with Infinite Health (Safe)) Health never goes down. Verified against the PAL ELF: the patched routine only touches the player object (fetched via the game's get-player function), so enemies are NOT affected. It refills the player's health from max health each time the death check runs.
patch=1,EE,20167D7C,extended,C441104C
patch=1,EE,20167D88,extended,E4411048

[Infinite Health (Safe)]
author=IRISHDEVELOPERDEV (custom, built and checked against the PAL ELF SLES_539.67)
description=[UNTESTED] Replacement for the Codejunkies Infinite Health (do not enable both). Every time the player takes damage, health is set back to full instead of going down, so the game never sees lethal damage and never starts the dying/downed state; knockdowns from explosions play out normally and you get back up. Enemies and NPCs take damage as normal. Scripted instant deaths (e.g. drowning, mission fail kills) are not blocked.
// Hook: 0x00239BE4 in the damage routine (0x00239AA8, health -= damage) was E6201048 swc1 $f0,0x1048($s1); now j 0x000C0200.
// Cave at 0x000C0200-0x000C023C: player = *(*(*(0x0059A260)+4)) - 0x1340 (same as the game's get-player function 0x00168490).
// If $s1 == player, $f0 = max health (+0x104C) before the store; otherwise the original store runs unchanged. Then j 0x00239BE8 (v2 fix 2026-10-30: v1 jumped to 0x239BEC and skipped "lw $v1,4($s3)", leaving a garbage pointer that froze the game).
patch=1,EE,200C0200,extended,3C02005A
patch=1,EE,200C0204,extended,8C42A260
patch=1,EE,200C0208,extended,1040000A
patch=1,EE,200C020C,extended,00000000
patch=1,EE,200C0210,extended,8C420004
patch=1,EE,200C0214,extended,10400007
patch=1,EE,200C0218,extended,00000000
patch=1,EE,200C021C,extended,8C420000
patch=1,EE,200C0220,extended,10400004
patch=1,EE,200C0224,extended,2442ECC0
patch=1,EE,200C0228,extended,14510002
patch=1,EE,200C022C,extended,00000000
patch=1,EE,200C0230,extended,C620104C
patch=1,EE,200C0234,extended,E6201048
patch=1,EE,200C0238,extended,0808E6FA
patch=1,EE,200C023C,extended,00000000
patch=1,EE,20239BE4,extended,08030080

[Infinite Ammo]
author=Codejunkies (AR MAX, decrypted by IRISHDEVELOPERDEV)
description=[UNTESTED] Spare ammo never goes down.
patch=1,EE,20156C54,extended,00000000

[No Reloads]
author=Codejunkies (AR MAX "Infinite Ammo/No Reloads", decrypted by IRISHDEVELOPERDEV)
description=[UNTESTED] The loaded clip never empties, so you never have to reload.
patch=1,EE,201582CC,extended,24420000

[Extort Business For 99 Million]
author=Codejunkies (AR MAX, decrypted by IRISHDEVELOPERDEV)
description=[UNTESTED] Max money. Verified against the PAL ELF: this patches the game's add-money routine, so the first time you earn (or spend) any money your cash jumps to about $99.9 million, and stays near that from then on.
patch=1,EE,2028C3F4,extended,3C0205F5

[Mob Vendetta Never Increases]
author=Codejunkies (AR MAX, decrypted by IRISHDEVELOPERDEV)
description=[UNTESTED] Rival families' vendetta level doesn't go up, so no mob wars from your actions.
patch=1,EE,20296FC4,extended,00000000

[Police Bribes Never Wear Off]
author=Codejunkies (AR MAX, decrypted by IRISHDEVELOPERDEV)
description=[UNTESTED] Once you bribe the police the bribe never runs down, keeping police heat off. Still cancelled if you commit a serious crime (e.g. killing a cop).
patch=1,EE,2029B520,extended,00000000

[Max Skill Points (Press L1+L2)]
author=Codejunkies (AR MAX, decrypted by IRISHDEVELOPERDEV)
description=[UNTESTED] (do not combine with the Always On version) Hold L1+L2 to set skill points to 100 so you can upgrade all skills. Only fires while L1+L2 are held.
patch=1,EE,E001FAFF,extended,00665C02
patch=1,EE,218085E8,extended,42C80000

[All Films Unlocked]
author=Codejunkies (AR MAX, decrypted by IRISHDEVELOPERDEV)
description=[UNTESTED] Unlocks all film clips in the Film Archive. Cosmetic only.
patch=1,EE,21B6908C,extended,42C80000
patch=1,EE,21B69190,extended,42C80000

[Max Skill Points (Always On)]
author=IRISHDEVELOPERDEV (v2 2026-10-31: pointer-safe rewrite, built and checked against the PAL ELF SLES_539.67; v1 was the Codejunkies L1+L2 code with the button check removed)
description=[UNTESTED] Keeps unspent skill points at 100, no button press. Open Pause > Skills and buy every upgrade; the points refill the next time the game reads them. v2 no longer writes to a fixed memory address: it only tops up the player's own "skill_points" stat, at the moment the game itself looks it up, so nothing is written on the title screen, during loading or before the player's stats exist. Never lowers points above 100. Do not enable together with the L1+L2 version.
// v1 was "patch=1,EE,218085E8,extended,42C80000": 100.0f written every frame to heap address 0x018085E8, which only holds the
//   skill_points value some of the time (title screen / loading / new-game setup = other data) -> possible freezes / bad saved data.
// Game facts (PAL ELF): stats live in a sorted table at *(obj+0x28) (count +8, 20-byte entries at +0x20: {hash, flags, float value @+8, ...}).
//   Skill points = stat hash 0x48EA4531 (lowercase x65599 of "skill_points"). The player's stats object is the singleton *(0x0059978C)
//   (set in its constructor 0x0028D0E8, zeroed in its destructor; the HUD, GetTotalSkillPoints 0x002CC248 and the upgrade code use it).
// Hook: 0x0028FB90 = stat lookup wrapper (only caller: stat-read routine 0x0028FBB0, before the Max All Skill Levels hook at 0x0028FBCC).
//   Was 27BDFFF0 addiu $sp,-0x10 / FFBF0000 sd $ra,0($sp); now j 0x000C0500 / nop (no branches target 0x0028FB94..0x0028FBAC).
// Cave 0x000C0500-0x000C0554 re-does the wrapper: own 0x10 stack frame, saves $ra and obj ($a0), calls the game's lookup 0x0028FB08.
//   Then only if entry != 0 AND hash ($a1, preserved by the lookup) == 0x48EA4531 AND obj == *(0x0059978C) AND value < 100.0f:
//   entry+8 = 100.0f (0x42C80000). Returns entry in $v0 exactly like the original; only $at/$t0-$t2 used (caller-saved, dead here).
patch=1,EE,200C0500,extended,27BDFFF0
patch=1,EE,200C0504,extended,FFBF0000
patch=1,EE,200C0508,extended,AFA40008
patch=1,EE,200C050C,extended,0C0A3EC2
patch=1,EE,200C0510,extended,00000000
patch=1,EE,200C0514,extended,1040000D
patch=1,EE,200C0518,extended,3C0148EA
patch=1,EE,200C051C,extended,34214531
patch=1,EE,200C0520,extended,14A1000A
patch=1,EE,200C0524,extended,8FA80008
patch=1,EE,200C0528,extended,3C09005A
patch=1,EE,200C052C,extended,8D29978C
patch=1,EE,200C0530,extended,15090006
patch=1,EE,200C0534,extended,3C0942C8
patch=1,EE,200C0538,extended,8C4A0008
